Contitution and Specs:

The Concept: A web app where users can log their daily media consumption (a book, a song, or a video game they checked out) 
alongside a chosen color palette or mood tag that represents their "vibe" for the day. Users can view a clean dashboard 
history of their past logs.

1. Objective

  To provide a lightweight, aesthetically pleasing digital journal where users can quickly log their daily media consumption 
  and emotional "vibe", helping them visualize patterns in their moods and media habits over time.

2. Behavior

  User Authentication: Users can securely log in or sign up for a personal account.

  Daily Log Creation: Users can submit a new entry consisting of a date, a media title, a category (book, music, game, movie), 
  a rating, and a primary vibe/mood tag.

  Data Visualization & Dashboard: The home screen displays a chronological feed of past entries and a simple summary chart showing 
  the distribution of logged moods or media categories.

3. Constraints

  The application must load and render responsive UI components on both desktop and mobile viewports.

  Data persistence must be handled via a relational database backend.

  Form inputs must validate against empty submissions or future dates.


4. Verification

  Test Case 1 (Creation): Submit a valid daily log entry and verify that it immediately appears in the 
  user's history feed and updates the dashboard metrics.

  Test Case 2 (Validation): Attempt to submit a log with missing required fields and verify that appropriate error 
  messages are displayed.

  Test Case 3 (Responsiveness): Resize the browser window from desktop to mobile dimensions to confirm that layout 
  elements stack correctly without horizontal overflow.


